  "description": "Imaging and the EHR personalise a coupled cardiorespiratory model: airway segmentation and estimated lung compliance parameterise a Pulse lung-mechanics model, while heart rate, pressures and labs parameterise a 0D OpenCOR cardiovascular model. An ensemble Kalman filter continuously assimilates the live ventilator and monitor signals — airway pressure, SpO2, end-tidal CO2 — so the twin stays locked to the patient in front of the clinician.\n\nThe twin then sweeps candidate PEEP and FiO2 settings, forecasts the resulting gas exchange with an uncertainty band, and surfaces an advisory recommendation — never a closed-loop action. It is advisory software: any real deployment would be regulated as Software as a Medical Device (IEC 62304, ISO 13485) and would need prospective clinical validation. Indicative budget EUR 150-300k for a research prototype (model coupling, assimilation pipeline, retrospective ICU-dataset validation); 6-9 months to a bench-validated twin, well before any clinical use.\n\nIllustrative output — a saved generation shown for display only, not a delivered project.",
